-- title:
--   Hasse germ at an end: j - a₀ is a unit times V^e
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ are primes with $\ell \ne q$, and $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $L$ is a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi \in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity.
--
--   **The function field.** The hypothesis `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the field of $q$-expansions attached to the level subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), where $H_1 =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   **The base ring.** $A$ is a henselian local discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, made into an algebra over which $K$ is a scalar tower over $L$; `hAq` requires $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and `hξA` that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$. The element $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **The chart.** $j \in K$ is non-zero and its Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras along their common middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. The ideal $y \subseteq C$ is maximal (`hy`), contains $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis is assumed at every closed point of $\mathfrak{X}$ over $\varpi$ lying over a supersingular point of the finite chart: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$, every $\varpi_z$ in the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase`, lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` and supersingular in the above sense (`hss'`, with $y'.asIdeal$ in place of $y$), it produces a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f -$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ is the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of the stalk, together with the conjunction of the following clauses, in which `toC` is the map from the stalk to its completion, `mkS` the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` the ring homomorphism from the finite chart algebra $C$ to the stalk at $z$ obtained from the germ along the open image of `ιFin`: (a) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (b) every $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$ — here `IsLevelAutAt` states that $\tau$ implements, on every element of $K$ whose Laurent expansion is a quotient of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of the given level and weight, the substitution by the matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` in $q$-expansions, read through any embedding $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$; (c) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.asIdeal$; (d) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.asIdeal$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the action of $\tau$ on $C$; $\theta$ fixing the classes of constants; $\theta(\overline{X_j}) \equiv \sum_i \overline{C(M_{ij})X_i}$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\overline{X_0}, \overline{X_1}$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (e) a branch-separation clause: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each omitting $\overline{X_0}$ or $\overline{X_1}$, each containing $\overline{C(\sigma\varpi)}$ and a class $\overline{C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h}$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (f) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above containing a class $\overline{C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h}$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (g) a Hasse clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the $j$-expansion with exponents scaled by $q\ell$ — lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $j_{q\ell} - a_0 \in y'.asIdeal$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a, b \in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(j_{q\ell}-a_0))) = \mathrm{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   **The fixed point and chart witness.** Data $z$, $\varpi_z$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), $y'$ (`hy'`) and `hss'` as above are fixed, with `hy'y` requiring $y'.asIdeal = y$. A particular witness $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1$ (with `hσ₁`, `hu₁`, `hv₁`, `hf₁` as in `hArig`) and isomorphism $e_1$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$ is fixed, and `hW₁` asserts for this witness the full conjunction (a)–(g) just described.
--
--   **The weighted centre and the blow-up algebra.** $J$ is an ideal of $C$, and `hJ` pins it as the infimum of all ideals of the form $\mathrm{comap}_{\tau|_C}\big(\mathrm{comap}_{e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}}\big(\overline{C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)}, \overline{X_0}, \overline{X_1}\big)\big)$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ and mapping $C$ into $C$. The subalgebra $B$ is pinned by `hB` as the $A$-algebra underlying $C\big[\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}\big]$.
--
--   **The exceptional valuation.** $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). `hR1` states that $C \le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator. `hR2` states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$; that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W$, i.e. $f \in W$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **The equivariance package `hEQ`** (five clauses, summarised here) requires: for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$, a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel is the set of elements of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and which, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ for $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, is equivariant for [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) along an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; that every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained by transporting the exceptional prime by some $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ carried into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by all such $\tau$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that any level automorphism for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The Hasse datum.** `hjK`, `hjC` place $j_{q\ell} =$ [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $K$ and in $C$; $a_0 \in A$ satisfies $j_{q\ell} - a_0 \in y$ (`ha₀`); $e_0 \ge 1$ (`he₀`) and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0} \subseteq W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ (`hh`) satisfy the leading-form unit condition `hhu` (for all $a, b \in W_1$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit) and `hgerm`: $e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(j_{q\ell}-a_0))) = \mathrm{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   **The local ring at the end.** $m \ge 1$ (`hm1`) satisfies $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hmt`). $O$ is a subring of $K$ and `hO` provides $a \in J$ with non-zero image in $K$ such that, with $B_a = C\big[\{x \in K : x a \in J\}\big]$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with: $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ ($f \in O$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$); no element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a unit of $O$; and $B$ is not contained in $O$. Further, $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and noetherian (`hOnoe`), $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`), and $\varpi \in O$ (`hϖO`). Elements $c_x, c_y \in O$ and a unit $u$ of $O$ are given, together with a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota : \widehat{O}_{\mathfrak{m}_O} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\big(\widehat{A}\big)\big(\varpi^m\big) = \widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(X_0X_1 - C(\varpi^m)\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{A}$ is the adic completion of $A$ and $\varpi$ denotes its image there, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model. The hypotheses are: $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ in $O$ (`hcxy`); $\iota$ sends the image of each $a \in A$ lying in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ in $\widehat{A}$ (`hιc`); $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ (`hιx`) and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$ (`hιy`), where $U$ and $V$ are the distinguished elements `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.V` of the model at the parameter $\varpi^m$; $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcyW`) and $c_x$ does not (`hcxW`), in each case whenever the element in question lies in $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The element $j_{q\ell} - a_0$ of $K$ lies in $O$, and there are a natural number $e$ with $e \ge 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model $\widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - C(\varpi^m))$ such that the image of $j_{q\ell} - a_0$ in the adic completion of $O$ satisfies
--   $$\iota\big(j_{q\ell} - a_0\big) \;=\; w_V \cdot V^{\,e},$$
--   with $V$ the distinguished element `UVCrossingModel.V` at the parameter $\varpi^m$.
--
--   This is the Katz–Mazur style statement that, at an end of the blown-up supersingular chart in characteristic $q$, the germ of the $j$-expansion minus its residue class is a unit multiple of a power of the branch parameter $V$, so that the Hasse invariant vanishes to exact order $e \ge 1$ along that branch. It is used by the assembly statements [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_cyclicDecomposition_ends_moduliHasse_igusaSepTranslate_commonChart_cover_blowupChart_linked_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_cyclicDecomposition_ends_moduliHasse_igusaSepTranslate_commonChart_cover_blowupChart_linked_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_mem_not_mem_span_U_const_of_mem_ends_crossing_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_mem_not_mem_span_U_const_of_mem_ends_crossing_linked).
